                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3433636f-7f35-3192-98a2-c1d0258cd93a",
                        "entry_id": "27f33fb5-eeac-37c3-b538-d1866388d224",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif aux chamans et au chamanisme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "813ad3c1-90e8-428b-8201-6f9e96307a0b",
                                "sense_id": "3433636f-7f35-3192-98a2-c1d0258cd93a",
                                "text": "Les rituels chamaniques."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff6d779a-3934-4f9b-b968-787075acca49",
                                "sense_id": "3433636f-7f35-3192-98a2-c1d0258cd93a",
                                "text": "Il se trouve que la ventriloquie, la glossolalie, le fait de parler les langues des animaux, le fait de simplement parler « en langues », ne caractérisent qu’un membre du couple chamanique. Georges Charachidzé rapporte que les Géorgiens du Caucase nomment celui qui parle dans la transe le « linguiste », tandis qu’ils appellent celui dont la possession est visuelle le « porte-étendard »."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c2386e92-daa5-415e-b1e7-32da85e4ef25",
                        "source_entry_id": "27f33fb5-eeac-37c3-b538-d1866388d224",
                        "source_sense_id": "3433636f-7f35-3192-98a2-c1d0258cd93a",
                        "target_lang_word": "shamanic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shamanic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e000c30f-1901-301c-ad7a-96b86e25da82",
                                        "entry_id": "eceff232-b79e-3cb9-8a17-362160816398",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to a shaman or to shamanism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5b83ea2-e705-4a1e-8a6e-c43c03d4c5aa",
                                                "sense_id": "e000c30f-1901-301c-ad7a-96b86e25da82",
                                                "text": "Ring sees both the NDE and UFOE as modern day shamanic initiations in which the journeyer (NDEer or UFOer) enters an \"imaginal\" reality, an alternative reality that coexists with physical reality and that is equally real."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b63483cc-4a0c-42a4-bf1e-cfaabb5f6011",
                        "source_entry_id": "27f33fb5-eeac-37c3-b538-d1866388d224",
                        "source_sense_id": "3433636f-7f35-3192-98a2-c1d0258cd93a",
                        "target_lang_word": "shamanistic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shamanistic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7ee466b8-42b3-3187-876c-b782a49a80e3",
                                        "entry_id": "86e5f127-0fb5-359e-9070-3f8cdceedc2c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, pertaining to, or characteristic of shamanism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10751f31-dcd6-4022-aafd-a2381d0923aa",
                                                "sense_id": "7ee466b8-42b3-3187-876c-b782a49a80e3",
                                                "text": "From Christ to the Fisher King of the Grail legends, the man suffering from a magical wound is no ordinary man; he is the man who has transcended the duality of sexuality, the man with a vulva, the shamanistic androgyne."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c820a5f-fe55-4a27-95f0-36024b645bf4",
                                                "sense_id": "7ee466b8-42b3-3187-876c-b782a49a80e3",
                                                "text": "There are an estimated 300 shamanistic temples within an hour of Seoul’s bustling city center, and in them, shamans perform their clamorous ceremonies every day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c223d82-f7bc-40d6-a6d2-e388316a4552",
                                                "sense_id": "7ee466b8-42b3-3187-876c-b782a49a80e3",
                                                "text": "In this film Ute Gebhardt looks at shamanistic healing rituals in Tuwa, which today is part of the Russian Federation. In Tuwa shamanism was able to survive five and a half decades of Soviet communism. Even today there is a shamanistic clinic in Tuwa’s capital Kyzyl."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
